# Technicomp Benchtop Linux: files that rpm does not install.
#
# htop, nvtop and atop are terminal programs, and amdgpu_top has a terminal
# interface besides its graphical one. Their launchers would put them in the
# GNOME app grid: htop's, nvtop's and amdgpu_top's come from upstream, atop's
# from openSUSE's package. Both of amdgpu_top's launchers are left out; the
# program itself stays installed, and amdgpu_top --gui still starts its
# graphical interface.
#
# The racket package (languages set) brings launchers for DrRacket and
# Slideshow, Racket's graphical IDE and presentation tool. Racket stays
# installed, and both still start from a terminal (drracket, slideshow).
#
# rpm documents this macro as "a colon separated list of paths where files
# should *not* be installed". rpm skips these paths on every install and update,
# records the files as not installed, and leaves them out of verification
# (rpm -V) and removal. The image build installs this file before all other
# packages (the bootstrap packages in config.kiwi), so the image never contains
# them either.
#
# A launcher that upstream renames is no longer matched and reappears; add its
# new path here. "rpm --eval %_netsharedpath" shows the list in effect.
%_netsharedpath /usr/share/applications/htop.desktop:/usr/share/applications/nvtop.desktop:/usr/share/applications/atop.desktop:/usr/share/applications/amdgpu_top-tui.desktop:/usr/share/applications/amdgpu_top.desktop:/usr/share/applications/drracket.desktop:/usr/share/applications/slideshow.desktop
